# Copy this file to .env.local (gitignored, see .gitignore's "# Env"
# section) and fill in real values. Used only by ops scripts under
# infrastructure/scripts/ that need to call the Cloudflare REST API
# directly (Workers AI / Vectorize) from a plain Node process outside
# the Workers runtime -- there is no live AI/VECTORIZE binding available
# there, same reasoning infrastructure/scripts/lib/d1-exec.mjs documents
# for why D1 access goes through `wrangler d1 execute` instead. Unlike
# D1 (which piggybacks on wrangler's own CLI login, no script-visible
# secret needed), Workers AI and Vectorize have no equivalent
# `wrangler ai run`/`wrangler vectorize upsert-via-http` passthrough for
# a one-off text embed from a script, so this is the one place a raw
# Cloudflare API token is unavoidable (confirmed against
# developers.cloudflare.com/workers-ai/models/bge-base-en-v1.5's own
# curl example and ArxivExplorer's scripts/debug-vectorize.ts, same
# account, same pattern -- no bespoke admin-secret layer invented here).
#
# Create a token at https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens with
# "Workers AI: Edit" and "Vectorize: Edit" permissions scoped to this
# account, nothing broader.
CF_TOKEN=
